{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4tJ4AcynfTRS5UFKidBLT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"units\": \"%lthr\" start end API format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"9822 convert training prescriptions to intervalsicu workouts with claude opus ai\",\"url\":\"https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"},{\"title\":\"icTrainer: Indoor Training - Now Supports HRM-Mode\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/ictrainer-indoor-training-now-supports-hrm-mode/52531\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a documented example of an HR step using `\"units\": \"%lthr\"` with `start`/`end` fields, so I can't confirm that exact format from these results.\n\n- **Undocumented JSON posting:** One forum user reported that posting the ICU JSON workout format works for HR and pace workouts, even though it isn't documented. Posting Intervals.icu text is the best way if you can because all features are supported. (Even though its not documented posting with JSON works.)\n- **Step format:** The sample JSON uses a `power` object with `value` and `units` (for example `%ftp`) inside each step. That's the power pattern, and the results don't show an HR equivalent. (forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7)\n- **Resolved start/end values:** A forum user found that resolved steps include a `_power` object with `start` and `end` fields, even when the step has no range. The developer confirmed that Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range. (forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20)\n- **HR range default:** For HR it is 1.5%. You can override this with the `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR in workout_doc:** The developer said LTHR and threshold pace were being added to `workout_doc`, with fields for `lthr`, `threshold_pace`, and `pace_units`. (forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)\n- **Target field:** Calendar events have a target field that is \"POWER\", \"HR\", \"PACE\" or \"AUTO\".\n- **Sending as % of LTHR:** One thread says the target HR is sent as % of LTHR when exchanged with Garmin, and that sending as % LTHR is done so that workouts can be exchanged with other users.\n\nFor the exact `%lthr` syntax, the official Intervals.icu API docs or a sample workout downloaded from the app (the forum suggests this approach) would be the most reliable check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b0b5f62-64dd-4e19-b449-ac0130fac058","uuid":"6e4fd758-7594-4ed2-95b1-59879ddd42ce","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:26:44.728Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"units\": \"%lthr\" start end API format","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Pcv6LXGj6Q8mpzvFZcmnQu","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu"