values:** A forum user found that resolved steps include a `_power` object with `start` and `end` fields, even when the step has no range. The developer confirmed that Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range. (forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20)\n- **HR range default:** For HR it is 1.5%. You can override this with the `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR in workout_doc:** The developer said LTHR and threshold pace were being added to `workout_doc`, with fields for `lthr`, `threshold_pace`, and `pace_units`. (forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)\n- **Target field:** Calendar events have a target field that is \"POWER\", \"HR\", \"PACE\" or \"AUTO\".\n- **Sending as % of LTHR:** One thread says the target HR is sent as % of LTHR when exchanged with Garmin, and that sending as % LTHR is done so that workouts can be exchanged with other users.\n\nFor the exact `%lthr` syntax, the official Intervals.icu API docs or a sample workout downloaded from the app (the forum suggests this approach) would be the most reliable check."],"durationSeconds":7.312190792000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T4tJ4AcynfTRS5UFKidBLT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
